0..76 Comment "// An update through an exclusive view of a held pair, answering as the copy"
77..94 Comment "// it stands for."
95..97 Comment "//"
98..173 Comment "// The view lends the held value, the body builds the new one, and `resume`"
174..252 Comment "// writes it back. The exclusivity conjecture says a runtime may build the new"
253..330 Comment "// value in the held value\'s own block when nothing else holds it. No program"
331..407 Comment "// can tell the difference, and these answers are what such a rebuild keeps."
408..410 Comment "//"
411..486 Comment "// Each item runs on both tiers. Normalisation by evaluation runs no memory"
487..560 Comment "// form, so the stated answers are the reference. A copy taken before the"
561..629 Comment "// update keeps its value, the independence the conjecture rests on."
630..632 Comment "//"
633..711 Comment "// - see: #3205 — not implemented: the rebuild in the held value\'s own block"
712..791 Comment "// - see: `crates/runtime-emitter/src/run.rs` — where the rebuild lands today"
792..866 Comment "// - see: Racordon, _A Formal Definition of Swift\'s Value Semantics_, 2020"
